        "R5"
      ],
      "text": "Calculated present action: trolley B4-B7 during 0-3, trolley B8-B11 during 3-6, hand carry B12 during 6-7. Inspect continuously in order, with B9 during 8-10. Boundary ordering permits whole-load unloading; the twelfth seal completes at 13. Predicted transfer occupation is seven minutes. Closest rival: consecutive hand trips 0-9 also permit completion at 13, with nine transfer minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "core_return_probe",
      "source_refs": [
        "O7",
        "U2",
        "R6",
        "R7",
        "O8"
      ],
      "text": "Hypothesis-level future intervention targets perceived replenishment cost: after identical successful service, expose delivery-associated occupied transfer minutes to later requesters. Sham/control presents the same ledger carrier identities with equal contact but without the effort association. Random assignment would compare later request frequency and carrier quantity per request while retaining identical initial demand and physical trolley service. This tests the hypothesized perception-to-request link, not present tool-dose harm. Later requester access and measurement are not supplied; the closed window cannot execute this probe."
    }
  ],
  "job_id": "DEV-S02-stage1",
  "policy": "S02",
  "residue": [
