  "tension": {
    "account_a": "Exogenous later-demand account: later production requirements determine request frequency and size independently of perceived trolley-service cost.",
    "account_b": "Tool-induced later-demand account: routine trolley service makes replenishment appear inexpensive, encouraging smaller, more frequent later requests; exposing effort can weaken that return link.",
    "prediction_a": "Under identical physical service, effort-linked disclosure and sham yield the same later request frequency and size.",
